WEBVTT

1
00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.934
There comes a time
for ever vampire...

2
00:01:32.104 --> 00:01:37.371
...when the idea of eternit becomes
momentaril unbearable.

3
00:01:37.576 --> 00:01:41.774
Living and feeding in the shadows
with onl our own compan...

4
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.973
...rots into a solitar.
hollow existence.

5
00:01:46.184 --> 00:01:48.812
Immortalit seems like a good idea...

6
00:01:49.254 --> 00:01:53.122
...until ou realize
ou're going to spend it alone.

7
00:01:53.325 --> 00:01:57.853
So I slept. hoping the sounds
of the passing eras would fade out...

8
00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:00.291
...and a sort of death might happen.

9
00:02:00.499 --> 00:02:05.163
But as I la there. the world didn't
sound like the place I had left...

10
00:02:05.671 --> 00:02:08.902
...but something different.

11
00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:11.567
Better....

12
00:02:43.141 --> 00:02:48.443
It became worthwhile to rise again
as new gods were born and worshiped.

13
00:02:48.647 --> 00:02:51.844
Night and da. the were never alone.

14
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.850
I would become one of them.

15
00:03:24.282 --> 00:03:28.480
Whether it was the meal or
the 100 ears of rest. I'm not sure.

16
00:03:28.687 --> 00:03:32.088
But suddenl
I was feeling better than ever.

17
00:03:32.357 --> 00:03:34.450
M senses so high...

18
00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:39.494
...the led me straight to the
instrument of m resurrection...

19
00:03:39.698 --> 00:03:43.634
...plaing in m old house.

20
00:04:12.664 --> 00:04:14.598
Jesus.

21
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:17.459
Your voice....

22
00:04:17.903 --> 00:04:19.336
Who the hell are you?

23
00:04:19.538 --> 00:04:23.975
The question provoked
an irresistible urge.

24
00:04:24.176 --> 00:04:27.111
l am the vampire Lestat.

25
00:04:27.312 --> 00:04:29.371
Itjust rolled out of m mouth.

26
00:04:29.581 --> 00:04:33.244
With one sentence.
I betraed everthing about m kind.

27
00:04:33.451 --> 00:04:35.476
Betraed our code of secrec.

28
00:04:35.687 --> 00:04:37.746
Vampire?

29
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.523
-That's funny.
-lndeed.

30
00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.251
Hilarious.

31
00:04:45.163 --> 00:04:47.131
You're all...

32
00:04:47.332 --> 00:04:49.027
...so beautiful.

33
00:04:49.568 --> 00:04:53.231
-Your hands are--
-Cold as death?

34
00:04:54.339 --> 00:04:56.500
-You're gonna kill us?
-No.

35
00:04:56.808 --> 00:05:01.643
All that you've ever dreamed of.
l'm going to make yours.

36
00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:04.475
This is your lucky day.

37
00:05:04.683 --> 00:05:07.049
It was a bold move. I admit.

38
00:05:07.252 --> 00:05:11.655
But from that moment on the were
m friends. m children. m band.

39
00:05:11.857 --> 00:05:15.418
Giving the world a new god.
Me.

40
00:07:06.571 --> 00:07:12.168
Okay. can l have your attention?
Okay. some questions. One at a time.

41
00:07:13.378 --> 00:07:15.938
-Yeah. you.
-So why here in London?

42
00:07:16.147 --> 00:07:18.741
We go where we're told to. like you.

43
00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:24.252
-How would you sum up your music?
-Sex. blood and rock and roll.

44
00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:26.584
Okay. excuse me.

45
00:07:27.892 --> 00:07:29.416
lt's time.

46
00:07:29.627 --> 00:07:31.288
May l present...

47
00:07:31.496 --> 00:07:35.193
...the vampire Lestat.

48
00:07:40.105 --> 00:07:41.333
Good evening.

49
00:07:42.841 --> 00:07:47.574
Sorr I'm late. I was just tring
to catch m breakfast.

50
00:07:50.348 --> 00:07:53.784
Okay. can we keep it short?
One at a time.

51
00:07:54.052 --> 00:07:55.246
Yeah. you.

52
00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.383
l may be wrong. but what
l remember about vampires is...

53
00:07:59.557 --> 00:08:02.651
...you generally keep
your identity secret.

54
00:08:02.861 --> 00:08:06.353
Yes. But wh hide it
in this da and age?

55
00:08:06.531 --> 00:08:09.193
I've hidden in the shadows
for centuries.

56
00:08:09.401 --> 00:08:12.131
It's time to share mself
with the world.

57
00:08:12.704 --> 00:08:17.539
Could you prove it? You know. give us
a demonstration of your powers.

58
00:08:17.742 --> 00:08:23.009
If ou like. I can give ou a private
demonstration in our hotel tonight.

59
00:08:27.085 --> 00:08:31.419
Your first and only concert's
in Death Valley. just days away.

60
00:08:31.623 --> 00:08:35.081
-Why just the one?
-I don't like repeating mself.

61
00:08:35.293 --> 00:08:40.162
There are rumors about
the hidden meaning in your lyrics...

62
00:08:40.331 --> 00:08:44.062
...that you're giving away
vampire secrets. ls that true?

63
00:08:44.269 --> 00:08:49.707
Mabe I'm tring to resurrect a few
old friends. Daring them to come out.

64
00:08:49.908 --> 00:08:54.345
Won't these vampires be pissed off
that you're giving away secrets?

65
00:08:54.979 --> 00:08:58.346
I imagine the are. es.

66
00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:02.145
Do you have anything to say
to the other vampires?

67
00:09:02.353 --> 00:09:05.413
As a matter of fact. I do.

68
00:09:06.991 --> 00:09:11.758
Come out. come out. wherever ou are.

69
00:09:13.531 --> 00:09:17.160
See ou all in Death Valle.

70
00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:44.023
l heard Lestat keeps all these girls
in his cellar. And it's nice.

71
00:09:44.229 --> 00:09:46.891
They give you food
and cable and weed.

72
00:09:47.098 --> 00:09:48.588
Oh. please.

73
00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:53.601
But you have to let him suck you
on your neck whenever he wants.

74
00:09:53.805 --> 00:09:56.968
-Doesn't sound too bad.
-Done worse.

75
00:09:57.175 --> 00:09:59.075
-l'll say.
-This way. girls.

76
00:10:12.624 --> 00:10:15.252
So this is Lestat's house?

77
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.793
lt is this week. We move around a lot.

78
00:10:18.997 --> 00:10:20.487
Why is that?

79
00:10:21.199 --> 00:10:24.430
What can l say? The guy is just....

80
00:10:26.037 --> 00:10:31.532
-Boss. l didn't see you there.
-No. You wouldn't. would you?

81
00:10:35.113 --> 00:10:38.549
These are the girls
that you asked for.

82
00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.808
Yes.

83
00:10:56.501 --> 00:10:59.664
Do you want me to take
the girls home later?

84
00:10:59.871 --> 00:11:02.032
No. thank you. Roger.

85
00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.902
l'll make sure they're taken care of.

86
00:11:07.679 --> 00:11:09.704
You want some?

87
00:11:10.715 --> 00:11:12.706
Want me?

88
00:11:13.718 --> 00:11:15.447
You hungry?

89
00:11:19.691 --> 00:11:23.218
You hungry for something else?

90
00:11:27.398 --> 00:11:29.127
Come on.

91
00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:33.092
-Don't you want to have some fun?
-Don't do that.

92
00:11:33.438 --> 00:11:35.804
Are you ticklish?

93
00:11:36.007 --> 00:11:38.669
l'm very ticklish.

94
00:12:44.742 --> 00:12:46.903
Come out. come out...

95
00:12:47.111 --> 00:12:49.545
...whoever you are.

96
00:12:57.722 --> 00:12:59.485
Jesse.

97
00:13:01.326 --> 00:13:04.489
Jesse.

98
00:13:04.696 --> 00:13:06.254
A voice...

99
00:13:07.165 --> 00:13:09.326
...calling to me...

100
00:13:09.534 --> 00:13:11.627
...in m dreams.

101
00:13:11.836 --> 00:13:15.499
The same dream I've had
since I was 6.

102
00:13:15.907 --> 00:13:18.774
I have a famil of m own.

103
00:13:19.077 --> 00:13:21.739
Not a strange dream. reall.

104
00:13:21.946 --> 00:13:24.676
One ever orphan has.

105
00:13:52.443 --> 00:13:54.308
l'm sorry. but you must go.

106
00:13:54.512 --> 00:13:58.312
Why can't l stay with you?
Please. Aunt Maharet.

107
00:13:58.516 --> 00:14:01.974
l don't want you to go. But you must.

108
00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:05.253
Aunt. you're bleeding.

109
00:14:11.963 --> 00:14:13.988
You must be with your own.

110
00:14:14.198 --> 00:14:18.862
-I knew things were not normal.
-This isn't the life I wanted for ou.

111
00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:23.166
I onl knew I was part of them.
and being cast out....

112
00:14:23.374 --> 00:14:24.671
Was I bad?

113
00:14:24.876 --> 00:14:26.969
Had I done something wrong?

114
00:14:27.178 --> 00:14:29.669
l'll always be watching over you.

115
00:14:29.881 --> 00:14:32.349
l want to stay with you forever.

116
00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:35.075
You can't.

117
00:15:10.855 --> 00:15:13.050
I'm Serena Altschul. MTV News.

118
00:15:13.257 --> 00:15:18.194
Vampire turned rocker Lestat
has returned with a new CD. Forsaken.

119
00:15:18.396 --> 00:15:20.387
Although from New Orleans...

120
00:15:20.598 --> 00:15:24.193
...he claims to be an 18th-centur
French nobleman...

121
00:15:24.368 --> 00:15:27.064
...who has been asleep
for over 100 ears.

122
00:15:27.271 --> 00:15:33.039
Here's a look at the new video
from the debut album. ''Redeemer. ''

123
00:16:41.746 --> 00:16:44.544
Like everone. I assumed
Lestat was a joke.

124
00:16:44.749 --> 00:16:49.880
A rock star with a gimmick. Then one
of his lyrics caught my attention.

125
00:16:50.221 --> 00:16:53.452
''Take a walk down the aisle
at the end of the mile.

126
00:16:53.624 --> 00:16:56.957
Give your life to my charms
in the Admiral's Arms.''

127
00:16:57.161 --> 00:16:58.685
That rang a bell.

128
00:16:58.896 --> 00:17:01.524
l tracked down old leases in London.

129
00:17:01.732 --> 00:17:05.896
lt turns out in the late 1 600s
there was a pub in Mile End...

130
00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.970
...called the Admiral's Arms.

131
00:17:08.172 --> 00:17:11.369
lt had a reputation for dealing
with black magic...

132
00:17:11.576 --> 00:17:14.136
...and reports of people vanishing.

133
00:17:14.345 --> 00:17:19.681
Here's where you could find
the Admiral's Arms in old London.

134
00:17:19.884 --> 00:17:22.876
That part of London
is mostly warehouses...

135
00:17:23.087 --> 00:17:27.217
...meat-packing plants and
a private club in the same location.

136
00:17:28.526 --> 00:17:31.962
l think that it's a vampire coven.

137
00:17:32.163 --> 00:17:34.961
And Lestat is leading us to it.

138
00:17:37.034 --> 00:17:40.128
-Who took this picture?
-l did.

139
00:17:40.338 --> 00:17:44.069
You're still an apprentice.
You don't do field work.

140
00:17:44.275 --> 00:17:45.902
The Talamasca has a code.

141
00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:49.739
l know. ''Observe the dark realm.
but be not of it.''

142
00:17:49.947 --> 00:17:52.882
Well. it's held good for 1 2 centuries.

143
00:17:53.084 --> 00:17:57.020
We record and observe.
but never interfere.

144
00:17:57.221 --> 00:17:59.314
l had to see it for myself.

145
00:18:02.226 --> 00:18:04.421
ls David aware of this?

146
00:18:04.962 --> 00:18:05.986
Jesse?

147
00:18:08.566 --> 00:18:09.555
Hello. David.

148
00:18:10.334 --> 00:18:14.065
-l was explaining--
-Why don't you see me in my office?

149
00:18:17.308 --> 00:18:20.471
This is a real coven.
ln the middle of London.

150
00:18:20.678 --> 00:18:24.011
All the more reason
to have told me first.

151
00:18:25.683 --> 00:18:27.310
Listen. Jesse...

152
00:18:30.788 --> 00:18:33.348
...we know about Lestat.

153
00:18:33.824 --> 00:18:36.554
What he's doing is unprecedented.

154
00:18:37.595 --> 00:18:39.187
So why is he doing it?

155
00:18:39.397 --> 00:18:42.992
Aren't you curious?
Don't you think we should find out?

156
00:18:44.435 --> 00:18:46.562
Let me show you something.

157
00:18:49.674 --> 00:18:51.574
What do you see?

158
00:18:54.278 --> 00:18:56.940
Mid-1 500s. Florence.

159
00:18:58.049 --> 00:18:59.607
This one?

160
00:19:03.421 --> 00:19:06.481
-This man is in both.
-Yes.

161
00:19:08.826 --> 00:19:11.192
All the different paint samples...

162
00:19:11.862 --> 00:19:13.762
...all authentic.

163
00:19:13.964 --> 00:19:17.593
Each painted at the time
of their particular style.

164
00:19:24.208 --> 00:19:26.369
His name is Marius.

165
00:19:27.244 --> 00:19:30.077
l've been tracing him for years.

166
00:19:30.548 --> 00:19:32.641
My little obsession.

167
00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.978
The closest we've come
to the original vampire.

168
00:19:36.253 --> 00:19:39.916
Marius himself dates back to 400 B.C.

169
00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.785
So he's older than Lestat.

170
00:19:45.996 --> 00:19:48.157
He made Lestat.

171
00:19:48.866 --> 00:19:50.231
How do you know that?

172
00:19:50.434 --> 00:19:53.301
Because l have Lestat's journal.

173
00:19:56.707 --> 00:19:58.174
l want to see it.

174
00:20:00.511 --> 00:20:03.571
Promise me you'll never
go back to that place.

175
00:20:34.912 --> 00:20:38.370
It was the winter of 1788.

176
00:20:38.582 --> 00:20:43.542
And I was brought to a Mediterranean
island b the man who made me.

177
00:20:44.855 --> 00:20:48.586
If a man is what ou'd call him.

178
00:21:38.108 --> 00:21:40.474
Lestat. welcome.

179
00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.013
Who are you?

180
00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:46.149
Do l know you?

181
00:21:48.686 --> 00:21:52.588
l am unknowable by nature.
but you may call me Marius.

182
00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:57.591
l'm the lord of a great manor.
They'll send an army to look for me.

183
00:21:57.795 --> 00:22:00.821
l doubt they'll find you.
Lord de Lioncourt.

184
00:22:01.031 --> 00:22:03.022
You're a long way from home.

185
00:22:32.263 --> 00:22:33.890
You're weak...

186
00:22:34.398 --> 00:22:35.865
...near passing.

187
00:22:37.668 --> 00:22:40.296
l can barely hear your heartbeat.

188
00:22:41.405 --> 00:22:46.707
The future hastens.
An age beyond my antique reason.

189
00:22:46.911 --> 00:22:49.880
You will help me understand
these times.

190
00:22:50.281 --> 00:22:52.374
That's why l chose you.

191
00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.274
Chose me for what?

192
00:23:04.194 --> 00:23:05.593
Drink...

193
00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:07.722
...and live.

194
00:23:08.699 --> 00:23:11.930
You've been brave enough
for one night. my son.

195
00:23:14.672 --> 00:23:16.833
Drink...

196
00:23:18.342 --> 00:23:20.333
...and learn.

197
00:23:22.713 --> 00:23:25.307
Good. is it not?

198
00:23:29.119 --> 00:23:31.644
No more. No more. Lestat.

199
00:23:33.123 --> 00:23:34.988
No more!

200
00:24:09.326 --> 00:24:11.726
Don't be afraid.

201
00:24:11.996 --> 00:24:15.022
lt's only your body that dies.

202
00:24:29.513 --> 00:24:31.845
More.

203
00:24:34.184 --> 00:24:37.745
I impressed m maker
with m thirst for things.

204
00:24:37.955 --> 00:24:40.583
He set out to educate me
in the unknown.

205
00:24:40.758 --> 00:24:45.388
Taught me all about the world.
its hidden histor...

206
00:24:45.596 --> 00:24:47.996
...and about mself.

207
00:24:53.470 --> 00:24:55.802
That's enough. my son.

208
00:24:58.675 --> 00:25:01.940
When you feed. hold back
from the moment of death.

209
00:25:02.146 --> 00:25:06.708
Never take the last drop. or it will
draw you in and you will die.

210
00:25:12.156 --> 00:25:14.454
Appreciate your prey.

211
00:25:19.596 --> 00:25:23.896
Their blood that we take into us
carries with it life...

212
00:25:24.101 --> 00:25:28.765
...their life. their knowledge.
their complexity.

213
00:25:31.809 --> 00:25:35.370
M senses run amuck.
like a newborn child.

214
00:25:36.213 --> 00:25:41.617
And as for m new powers. I was beside
mself with the pleasure of it all.

215
00:25:44.121 --> 00:25:45.782
We've stayed long enough.

216
00:25:45.989 --> 00:25:47.786
But we've spoken to no one.

217
00:25:48.358 --> 00:25:51.122
A vampire's life
is a life of discretion.

218
00:25:51.328 --> 00:25:52.920
Discretion?

219
00:25:53.597 --> 00:25:55.565
Why must we hide. Marius?

220
00:25:55.766 --> 00:25:59.099
We are the powerful.
we are the immortal.

221
00:25:59.303 --> 00:26:02.795
We should walk fearless
in the open. no?

222
00:26:13.517 --> 00:26:15.781
That cannot be.

223
00:26:16.787 --> 00:26:19.483
We're vulnerable during the day.

224
00:26:19.690 --> 00:26:23.820
Mortals must never know about us.
for the sake of all our kind.

225
00:26:24.328 --> 00:26:26.489
So l could never know her?

226
00:26:26.697 --> 00:26:29.029
Not unless you wanted to kill her.

227
00:26:36.340 --> 00:26:38.171
So l can never be known?

228
00:26:40.844 --> 00:26:43.642
You must be dead to the world.

229
00:26:44.848 --> 00:26:47.214
Come on. time to leave.

230
00:27:48.212 --> 00:27:50.476
Sophia. run! Run!

231
00:27:50.814 --> 00:27:53.180
Go! Go--

232
00:27:54.017 --> 00:27:55.279
Lestat...

233
00:27:55.485 --> 00:27:57.783
...stop her!

234
00:27:58.555 --> 00:27:59.613
You must!

235
00:28:37.227 --> 00:28:41.129
We must remain in the shadows.

236
00:28:42.566 --> 00:28:46.127
You still have a few
lingering mortal emotions.

237
00:28:47.237 --> 00:28:50.570
They'll serve you no good. my friend.

238
00:29:03.153 --> 00:29:05.087
Forgive me.

239
00:29:12.129 --> 00:29:18.193
The faces of m victims haunted me.
reminding me of m fate.

240
00:29:18.402 --> 00:29:20.768
For nights and das I plaed...

241
00:29:20.971 --> 00:29:26.705
...furious that I would never partake
of the simplejos of the world.

242
00:29:26.910 --> 00:29:29.105
I was meant for more than this.

243
00:30:08.719 --> 00:30:10.619
Marius?

244
00:31:32.035 --> 00:31:34.663
Would you like me to play for you?

245
00:34:02.686 --> 00:34:05.280
What have you done. Lestat?

246
00:34:14.598 --> 00:34:18.295
-More!
-l don't think so. my little lord.

247
00:34:18.535 --> 00:34:20.560
-Let me go.
-No.

248
00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:24.228
You've had the purest blood.
seen the oldest things.

249
00:34:24.441 --> 00:34:29.902
-Far too much for one as young as you.
-Her blood is like liquid fire.

250
00:34:30.113 --> 00:34:31.512
Who is she?

251
00:34:36.953 --> 00:34:39.080
She's your mother.

252
00:34:39.289 --> 00:34:41.348
She's my mother.

253
00:34:41.558 --> 00:34:45.722
Akasha. the queen of all
who are damned.

254
00:34:46.363 --> 00:34:48.297
And he's her king.

255
00:34:48.798 --> 00:34:53.997
Akasha and Enkil nearly drank this
earth dry when they ruled over Egypt.

256
00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:58.163
They drank until Enkil
lost his will to drink.

257
00:34:58.341 --> 00:35:03.301
Without her mate beside her. she also
lost hers. They became living statues.

258
00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:09.112
She respects nothing except the taste
of blood. human and immortal alike.

259
00:35:09.486 --> 00:35:11.010
No. Release me!

260
00:35:17.093 --> 00:35:19.493
She made you quite powerful.

261
00:35:19.663 --> 00:35:21.893
You'll not stop me!

262
00:35:23.166 --> 00:35:26.033
Can l hear her blood in your voice?

263
00:35:26.836 --> 00:35:30.363
ln all the years of my care.
not once have they moved.

264
00:35:30.573 --> 00:35:34.270
Until tonight. And she chose me.

265
00:35:35.178 --> 00:35:36.805
l chose you.

266
00:35:40.850 --> 00:35:44.183
Where are you going?! Marius!

267
00:36:41.611 --> 00:36:47.948
Man times since. I have called
to Marius. But there was no answer.

268
00:36:48.485 --> 00:36:52.979
Just the endless procession
of das. months...

269
00:36:53.156 --> 00:36:54.680
...ears.

270
00:36:55.859 --> 00:36:59.522
M teacher left me
to m darkest lesson.

271
00:36:59.696 --> 00:37:01.857
That in the end. we are alone.

272
00:37:02.766 --> 00:37:08.727
And there is nothing but the cold.
dark wasteland of eternit.

273
00:37:33.630 --> 00:37:37.088
David thought thejournal
would satisf m curiosit.

274
00:37:37.767 --> 00:37:40.964
But it onl made me want
to know more.

275
00:37:41.137 --> 00:37:43.833
I had to go back
to the Admiral's Arms.

276
00:37:44.007 --> 00:37:46.441
I had no choice.

277
00:38:22.946 --> 00:38:25.938
This is a fantastic place. I love it.

278
00:38:26.616 --> 00:38:29.380
You sure l can't get you a drink?

279
00:38:30.353 --> 00:38:31.650
Soon.

280
00:39:34.317 --> 00:39:35.875
Hi.

281
00:39:36.753 --> 00:39:38.152
-Hi.
-Come here often?

282
00:39:38.588 --> 00:39:40.351
All the time.

283
00:39:44.193 --> 00:39:47.060
l don't see any marks.

284
00:39:47.230 --> 00:39:49.755
You haven't seen the rest of my body.

285
00:39:50.767 --> 00:39:53.395
ls that an invitation?

286
00:39:53.569 --> 00:39:55.662
Sorry. l'm taken.

287
00:39:55.872 --> 00:39:57.669
And...

288
00:39:58.374 --> 00:40:00.433
...where is your host?

289
00:40:00.843 --> 00:40:02.208
He's here somewhere.

290
00:40:05.915 --> 00:40:09.510
This host. what's his name?

291
00:40:13.556 --> 00:40:14.853
Marius.

292
00:40:15.758 --> 00:40:18.488
Sorry. don't know the guy.

293
00:40:18.661 --> 00:40:23.098
-Of course not. He's an ancient.
-There aren't any ancients left.

294
00:40:23.266 --> 00:40:25.928
They all turned to dust.

295
00:40:26.269 --> 00:40:29.500
So unless you've got him in a bottle
somewhere....

296
00:40:29.672 --> 00:40:32.766
You're brave to joke.
l wish you could meet him.

297
00:40:32.942 --> 00:40:36.537
-And why is that?
-Because you might learn something.

298
00:40:40.016 --> 00:40:42.007
Excuse me.

299
00:40:56.399 --> 00:40:58.094
Going somewhere?

300
00:41:00.003 --> 00:41:02.972
Now this will only hurt a little bit.

301
00:41:03.373 --> 00:41:07.207
ln fact. you might even enjoy it.

302
00:41:07.410 --> 00:41:08.434
Don't do this.

303
00:41:29.065 --> 00:41:30.555
Boo.

304
00:41:46.115 --> 00:41:49.482
That was quite a performance.

305
00:41:50.119 --> 00:41:52.883
You should be more careful.

306
00:41:54.023 --> 00:41:57.322
-Thanks.
-For what?

307
00:41:57.660 --> 00:41:59.491
You saved me.

308
00:42:00.163 --> 00:42:02.154
How presumptuous.

309
00:42:03.066 --> 00:42:06.593
So you know Marius?

310
00:42:08.871 --> 00:42:10.532
l know a lot of things.

311
00:42:10.740 --> 00:42:13.402
Not how to stay alive. apparently.

312
00:42:13.743 --> 00:42:15.904
l guess we have that in common.

313
00:42:16.446 --> 00:42:19.381
Although l'm a little ahead
of the race here.

314
00:42:19.582 --> 00:42:22.107
Well. l can fix that.

315
00:42:22.752 --> 00:42:27.086
Your song ''Redeemer'' is about
the girl with the violin. lsn't it?

316
00:42:28.791 --> 00:42:29.951
Yeah.

317
00:42:30.193 --> 00:42:31.592
ls it?

318
00:42:34.564 --> 00:42:36.828
What else do you think you know?

319
00:42:37.934 --> 00:42:39.196
l....

320
00:42:39.402 --> 00:42:41.870
You're shaking.

321
00:42:42.071 --> 00:42:43.470
Cold.

322
00:42:44.474 --> 00:42:46.032
Still cold?

323
00:42:47.610 --> 00:42:51.546
Go on. Tell me more about me.

324
00:42:51.781 --> 00:42:53.408
You want....

325
00:42:53.616 --> 00:42:55.550
What do l want?

326
00:42:56.953 --> 00:43:00.389
-You yearn.
-What do l yearn?

327
00:43:03.759 --> 00:43:06.523
For what do l yearn?

328
00:43:06.696 --> 00:43:08.823
To walk with the living.

329
00:43:10.433 --> 00:43:14.893
Out of the cold.
dark wasteland of eternity.

330
00:43:18.407 --> 00:43:19.465
Well...

331
00:43:21.911 --> 00:43:25.244
...that makes you
a very clever librarian.

332
00:43:25.414 --> 00:43:27.974
Talamasca.

333
00:43:28.151 --> 00:43:31.643
l knew l left that journal somewhere.

334
00:43:34.490 --> 00:43:38.358
-Was it a good read?
-lt touched me.

335
00:43:38.961 --> 00:43:40.622
Did it. now?

336
00:43:42.064 --> 00:43:43.929
Don't worry. Jesse.

337
00:43:44.367 --> 00:43:46.961
Your kind never satisfies my thirst.

338
00:43:49.972 --> 00:43:53.339
Lestat. l know something
that's not in your journal.

339
00:43:55.912 --> 00:43:56.901
What?

340
00:43:57.446 --> 00:43:59.880
You still have the violin. don't you?

341
00:44:00.550 --> 00:44:02.609
No. l understand.

342
00:44:03.553 --> 00:44:05.316
After all. it's only human.

343
00:45:02.011 --> 00:45:04.002
Clever librarian.

344
00:45:14.223 --> 00:45:18.091
David. listen. l'm going
to Los Angeles for the concert.

345
00:45:18.794 --> 00:45:21.854
I met him. David. I talked to Lestat.

346
00:45:22.131 --> 00:45:24.326
What? Jesse?

347
00:45:24.533 --> 00:45:28.094
Listen to me very carefully now.

348
00:45:29.739 --> 00:45:32.708
You are no longer seeing
things clearly.

349
00:45:32.875 --> 00:45:36.641
Lestat told the world that vampires
live among us. The're mad.

350
00:45:36.812 --> 00:45:41.374
The'll be at the concert to kill him.
You've become obsessed with it.

351
00:45:41.550 --> 00:45:46.283
-I'm worried about ou.
-Don't worry about me. l'll be okay.

352
00:45:46.489 --> 00:45:48.389
l'll check in and....

353
00:45:49.458 --> 00:45:51.085
l'm sorry. l have to go.

354
00:45:51.294 --> 00:45:52.886
No. Jesse--

355
00:46:09.712 --> 00:46:13.705
The cit of Lost Angels alread
fed on the blood of outh.

356
00:46:13.883 --> 00:46:17.148
M presence here barel
stirred a ripple.

357
00:46:17.320 --> 00:46:19.720
We had three das till the concert.

358
00:46:19.922 --> 00:46:22.447
I could feel something was coming.

359
00:46:22.625 --> 00:46:25.788
Ijust couldn't figure out what.

360
00:46:58.627 --> 00:47:00.151
Marius.

361
00:47:12.208 --> 00:47:13.971
Lestat.

362
00:47:15.344 --> 00:47:17.812
lt is good to see you. Lestat.

363
00:47:19.115 --> 00:47:20.480
And you.

364
00:47:20.716 --> 00:47:24.345
Still wearing the old fashions. l see.

365
00:47:26.155 --> 00:47:28.316
Old habits die hard.

366
00:47:28.524 --> 00:47:33.655
How did you manage to slip
through the '50s in red velvet?

367
00:47:34.363 --> 00:47:35.830
l slept.

368
00:47:37.199 --> 00:47:39.463
Don't think you missed much.

369
00:47:40.669 --> 00:47:44.366
-Elvis.
-Elvis. yes.

370
00:47:46.575 --> 00:47:48.600
You're bigger than he is now.

371
00:47:49.011 --> 00:47:50.035
So....

372
00:47:50.913 --> 00:47:53.040
After all this time...

373
00:47:53.582 --> 00:47:55.516
...what's the occasion?

374
00:47:55.684 --> 00:48:01.213
You've just become very hard to avoid
these days. at least in conversation.

375
00:48:02.224 --> 00:48:05.751
-What are you trying to prove. Lestat?
-Oh. please.

376
00:48:05.928 --> 00:48:10.160
lt's a little too late to come over
all paternal now. Marius.

377
00:48:10.366 --> 00:48:14.132
Two hundred years
and not a word from you.

378
00:48:15.371 --> 00:48:18.465
You almost cost me everything.

379
00:48:21.410 --> 00:48:23.037
Now you've done it again.

380
00:48:23.646 --> 00:48:27.207
This isn't the time to settle
old scores.

381
00:48:28.851 --> 00:48:31.911
Vampires don't settle old scores.

382
00:48:34.023 --> 00:48:36.457
We harbor them.

383
00:48:40.763 --> 00:48:42.526
How did you find me?

384
00:48:43.098 --> 00:48:44.463
l made you.

385
00:48:44.800 --> 00:48:47.132
l've always known where you are.

386
00:48:47.937 --> 00:48:49.404
Besides...

387
00:48:49.738 --> 00:48:54.004
...l just had to look for the most
gauche house on the block.

388
00:48:55.678 --> 00:48:59.546
Come. Let me show you what it means
to live in the light.

389
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:10.250
lmpressive.

390
00:00:10.421 --> 00:00:14.824
Reminds me of old mad druids
running around chanting in the forest.

391
00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:17.119
A return to the primitive.

392
00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:19.787
Out there. my fans...

393
00:00:21.099 --> 00:00:22.657
...they worship me.

394
00:00:23.101 --> 00:00:28.198
Millions of arms reach out to embrace.
beg me to come into their lives.

395
00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:30.397
lt's what you always wanted.

396
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:33.270
With all my black little heart.

397
00:00:34.612 --> 00:00:37.945
Did you think of anyone but yourself?

398
00:00:38.349 --> 00:00:41.614
l only have myself.
You taught me that.

399
00:00:42.353 --> 00:00:45.754
lt may be time to get ready
for some company.

400
00:00:45.923 --> 00:00:51.555
-What's that supposed to mean?
-Your music's woken an old friend.

401
00:00:53.564 --> 00:00:55.191
Can't you hear it?

402
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.261
Or is the applause all you
can hear now?

403
00:01:18.389 --> 00:01:19.720
Akasha.

404
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:22.117
Arisen.

405
00:01:22.827 --> 00:01:25.591
She has taken the king's blood.

406
00:01:25.863 --> 00:01:27.763
Absorbed his power.

407
00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:31.493
Good. Let her come.

408
00:01:31.836 --> 00:01:33.963
Cancel the concert.

409
00:01:34.272 --> 00:01:35.603
Never.

410
00:01:36.207 --> 00:01:40.166
You're no match for her. Lestat.
You're not a god.

411
00:01:40.845 --> 00:01:43.643
We were once mortals too.

412
00:01:44.682 --> 00:01:47.515
lt is our heritage we protect.

413
00:01:47.685 --> 00:01:50.483
Such reverence for mortals.

414
00:01:50.688 --> 00:01:53.623
Then you should have left me as one.

415
00:02:54.352 --> 00:02:59.688
Scent is fading.
He was here too long ago.

416
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.619
You like him. do you?

417
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.785
He reminds me of someone.

418
00:03:04.996 --> 00:03:09.660
All he's going to remind you of soon
is a pile of bones.

419
00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:13.062
We're going to dismember him.
Bleed him dry.

420
00:03:13.237 --> 00:03:14.431
Really?

421
00:03:15.673 --> 00:03:19.109
ls that what you're going to do?

422
00:06:17.455 --> 00:06:20.913
Old gods on new streets.

423
00:06:21.425 --> 00:06:24.917
Not onl had the concert sold out
among the living...

424
00:06:25.095 --> 00:06:28.223
...it seemed all the undead
were coming too.

425
00:06:28.432 --> 00:06:31.333
There would be angr vampires
out there...

426
00:06:31.502 --> 00:06:35.666
...frightened of the light I was
directing on all our kind.

427
00:06:35.873 --> 00:06:39.434
Do ou have anthing to sa
to the other vampires?

428
00:06:39.643 --> 00:06:43.477
Yes. as a matter of fact. I do.

429
00:06:44.381 --> 00:06:47.817
Come out. come out. wherever ou are.

430
00:06:48.552 --> 00:06:50.645
The wanted me dead.

431
00:06:50.855 --> 00:06:52.516
Let them tr.

432
00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.357
Bring it on.

433
00:06:54.758 --> 00:06:57.556
Better dead than alone.

434
00:07:13.244 --> 00:07:15.769
Hey. honey. Want tickets for tomorrow?

435
00:07:15.946 --> 00:07:17.777
-Going to the show?
-No.

436
00:07:17.948 --> 00:07:21.714
-Come on. l got them for $200.
-$200?! l don't think so.

437
00:07:21.886 --> 00:07:27.791
-What if l say 1 50?
-1 50? You're gonna cut me a deal?

438
00:07:27.992 --> 00:07:32.190
So. listen. just two girls. okay?
So how old are you again?

439
00:07:35.165 --> 00:07:38.430
-Check it out. Champagne?
-Yeah.

440
00:07:55.619 --> 00:08:00.716
Oh. my God. l can't believe
it's really you! l'm your biggest fan.

441
00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.159
Boo.

442
00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:06.426
Boo back.

443
00:08:07.331 --> 00:08:09.959
Lestat. l came all the way
from Tarzana.

444
00:08:10.134 --> 00:08:11.260
Really?

445
00:08:12.269 --> 00:08:13.861
-And you?
-London.

446
00:08:15.139 --> 00:08:17.733
A London Goth. l see.

447
00:08:18.842 --> 00:08:23.541
lt's funny. l would have pegged you
for a Talamascan.

448
00:08:24.481 --> 00:08:26.415
Maybe in another life.

449
00:08:26.584 --> 00:08:28.211
l'm an Episcopalian.

450
00:08:28.686 --> 00:08:32.213
And l'm a frigging Buddhist.
Lestat....

451
00:08:32.389 --> 00:08:36.723
Roger. would you take our little
Episcopalian back to church?

452
00:08:36.894 --> 00:08:39.454
Just the one tonight? Sure.

453
00:08:39.663 --> 00:08:42.928
-Sweetheart. come on.
-What?

454
00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:45.228
-Come on.
-What?!

455
00:08:45.402 --> 00:08:48.599
-lt's a good thing.
-Can l still go backstage?

456
00:08:50.341 --> 00:08:52.901
Why are you following me?

457
00:08:53.177 --> 00:08:54.576
What do you want?

458
00:09:08.058 --> 00:09:12.392
So you come all this way
just to return this to me?

459
00:09:12.596 --> 00:09:15.565
Out of the goodness of your heart?

460
00:09:18.235 --> 00:09:20.897
l want you to show me what it's like.

461
00:09:21.305 --> 00:09:24.433
What what is like. exactly?

462
00:09:24.608 --> 00:09:26.769
To be like you.

463
00:09:29.813 --> 00:09:31.906
l don't have time for this.

464
00:09:32.316 --> 00:09:36.548
-All a vampire has is time.
-Not this one.

465
00:09:38.489 --> 00:09:39.717
Right.

466
00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:42.652
The covens are coming for you.

467
00:09:42.826 --> 00:09:47.525
How are you going to spend your last
night. as you always have. alone?

468
00:09:47.698 --> 00:09:48.926
Why not?

469
00:09:49.667 --> 00:09:52.033
Why not share it with me?

470
00:09:55.939 --> 00:09:57.406
All right.

471
00:10:00.144 --> 00:10:03.545
This may be painful for a mortal.

472
00:10:03.747 --> 00:10:06.875
You're still attached to your skin.

473
00:10:07.951 --> 00:10:09.646
l don't care.

474
00:10:12.256 --> 00:10:14.053
Do you trust me?

475
00:10:17.861 --> 00:10:19.351
Yes.

476
00:10:28.505 --> 00:10:30.871
Then close your eyes.

477
00:11:48.285 --> 00:11:50.253
Marius was right.

478
00:11:50.454 --> 00:11:53.617
But l never understood
until l met you.

479
00:11:54.191 --> 00:11:56.216
What do you mean?

480
00:11:56.393 --> 00:11:59.794
You're beautiful to me
because you're human.

481
00:11:59.963 --> 00:12:02.090
Your frailty...

482
00:12:02.366 --> 00:12:04.300
...your short years...

483
00:12:06.737 --> 00:12:08.398
...your heart...

484
00:12:08.605 --> 00:12:11.438
...even as you think it's breaking.

485
00:12:15.813 --> 00:12:17.610
All that...

486
00:12:19.049 --> 00:12:23.713
...seems suddenly more precious
than anything l have ever known.

487
00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.823
l'm not as precious as you think.

488
00:12:39.269 --> 00:12:40.702
Do it.

489
00:12:44.274 --> 00:12:45.764
Please.

490
00:12:52.049 --> 00:12:54.279
Let me be with you.

491
00:12:56.587 --> 00:12:59.181
Let me know everything.

492
00:13:07.297 --> 00:13:09.822
You want to know everything?

493
00:13:11.935 --> 00:13:13.527
Come. then.

494
00:13:13.804 --> 00:13:15.601
l'll show you.

495
00:13:38.028 --> 00:13:40.553
What is it? What are we doing--?

496
00:14:26.343 --> 00:14:27.901
ls she all right?

497
00:14:32.249 --> 00:14:35.412
Get away! Get off me!

498
00:14:44.127 --> 00:14:45.754
Now you see?

499
00:14:46.296 --> 00:14:47.729
Are you ready?

500
00:14:49.533 --> 00:14:52.798
Now do you want it. huh?

501
00:14:55.872 --> 00:14:56.998
No.

502
00:14:57.407 --> 00:15:00.103
Of course you don't.

503
00:15:59.403 --> 00:16:02.201
They're pretty worked-up.
How you feeling?

504
00:16:02.372 --> 00:16:04.101
Hey. girls. come on!

505
00:16:05.342 --> 00:16:08.505
Okay. through here. Let him through!

506
00:16:08.945 --> 00:16:10.344
Back off. fella!

507
00:16:10.547 --> 00:16:12.014
Come on. children.

508
00:16:12.215 --> 00:16:14.376
Okay. guys. Come on!

509
00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.688
Let him through.

510
00:16:24.261 --> 00:16:25.660
Jesse!

511
00:16:28.265 --> 00:16:29.562
Jesse!

512
00:16:33.437 --> 00:16:34.904
Hello. David.

513
00:16:36.006 --> 00:16:39.339
l must show you my new
paintings sometime.

514
00:19:02.485 --> 00:19:03.679
Find Jesse.

515
00:19:52.135 --> 00:19:54.103
You want more?

516
00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.909
This one's for those
who've come for me.

517
00:23:01.724 --> 00:23:02.986
Akasha.

518
00:24:22.639 --> 00:24:24.664
Akasha?!

519
00:24:25.308 --> 00:24:27.868
Why so surprised. my love?

520
00:24:28.645 --> 00:24:30.704
You called. l have come.

521
00:24:31.781 --> 00:24:32.839
My love?

522
00:24:33.349 --> 00:24:35.909
Never fear me. Lestat.

523
00:24:36.986 --> 00:24:39.216
All your wishes have come true.

524
00:24:39.389 --> 00:24:41.050
My wishes?

525
00:24:43.259 --> 00:24:46.820
For a companion to share eternity.

526
00:24:49.365 --> 00:24:53.267
You're bold. like your music.

527
00:24:55.138 --> 00:25:00.075
You live your life in the open.
like l did long ago...

528
00:25:01.244 --> 00:25:03.007
...when l had a king.

529
00:25:03.513 --> 00:25:04.673
Had a king?

530
00:25:05.114 --> 00:25:06.809
He's no more.

531
00:25:07.584 --> 00:25:11.042
Now you are my consort.

532
00:25:12.021 --> 00:25:14.182
That's why l kept you safe.

533
00:25:15.325 --> 00:25:16.849
Alive.

534
00:25:17.860 --> 00:25:19.350
You?

535
00:25:21.097 --> 00:25:23.895
You thought it was all you?

536
00:25:27.036 --> 00:25:30.096
The ego of a king as well.

537
00:25:30.306 --> 00:25:31.796
Yes.

538
00:25:33.076 --> 00:25:36.409
l know you. Lestat.

539
00:25:36.813 --> 00:25:40.874
l know that you crave to have
the world at your feet.

540
00:25:42.385 --> 00:25:45.843
And l have come to give it to you.

541
00:25:47.790 --> 00:25:49.758
Where are we?

542
00:25:50.627 --> 00:25:52.561
We are home.

543
00:25:53.129 --> 00:25:58.362
We live everwhere
and anwhere we choose.

544
00:25:58.768 --> 00:26:02.499
The world is our garden.

545
00:28:27.316 --> 00:28:31.446
All these ears I'd hoped
this place was real.

546
00:28:33.623 --> 00:28:38.959
For the first time in m life.
I feel like I'm home.

547
00:28:39.529 --> 00:28:43.590
Strange that this journe
should lead me here.

548
00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:47.031
This place that's haunted m dreams.

549
00:28:52.408 --> 00:28:55.241
Aunt. ou're bleeding.

550
00:28:55.444 --> 00:28:57.674
You must be with our own.

551
00:29:00.283 --> 00:29:02.808
I'll alwas be watching over ou.

552
00:29:03.019 --> 00:29:05.749
I want to sta with ou forever.

553
00:29:06.956 --> 00:29:09.447
Forever is a very long time.

554
00:29:12.795 --> 00:29:14.422
Aunt Maharet.

555
00:29:24.473 --> 00:29:28.034
You haven't aged.
you haven't changed at all.

556
00:29:30.980 --> 00:29:33.312
l was once a mortal too.

557
00:29:33.649 --> 00:29:37.779
l bore a child before Akasha took me.
l took care of that child...

558
00:29:37.954 --> 00:29:41.617
...and her children.
and her children's children.

559
00:29:42.191 --> 00:29:44.455
This is our family.

560
00:29:44.627 --> 00:29:47.187
My way of coping with eternity.

561
00:29:49.232 --> 00:29:54.067
You are what keeps me connected
to the world of the living.

562
00:29:54.737 --> 00:29:58.867
When your parents died. l brought
you here to take care of you.

563
00:30:04.380 --> 00:30:07.144
Now is not the time.

564
00:30:08.551 --> 00:30:12.317
You were seeking answers
and now you've found them.

565
00:30:12.722 --> 00:30:16.453
The family is who you are.

566
00:31:47.450 --> 00:31:51.614
Drinking my blood allows you
to live in the light.

567
00:31:51.821 --> 00:31:56.758
And soon the sun will no longer
sting your eyes.

568
00:31:57.960 --> 00:32:02.454
This is but a taste
of what we shall share. my love.

569
00:32:03.599 --> 00:32:05.294
My king...

570
00:32:06.135 --> 00:32:09.036
...behold our kingdom.

571
00:32:09.672 --> 00:32:12.038
A kingdom of corpses?

572
00:32:14.043 --> 00:32:17.444
-Why?
-Why not?

573
00:32:18.114 --> 00:32:19.911
This is why you have risen?

574
00:32:20.082 --> 00:32:23.415
They believed in nothing.

575
00:32:23.819 --> 00:32:25.377
Now they are nothing.

576
00:32:32.061 --> 00:32:35.121
But you and l.
we will change all that.

577
00:32:36.332 --> 00:32:41.065
We will give the world something
to believe in again.

578
00:32:42.204 --> 00:32:44.297
Now come. my love.

579
00:32:44.707 --> 00:32:46.766
We have a score to settle.

580
00:32:58.854 --> 00:33:01.516
Since my mortal death.
l have watched...

581
00:33:02.224 --> 00:33:06.524
...l have guided and cared
for my human family...

582
00:33:07.063 --> 00:33:09.964
...generations beyond memory.

583
00:33:12.068 --> 00:33:15.731
This is why we must fight Akasha.

584
00:33:17.073 --> 00:33:21.874
-For the sake of your great family.
-The world we know is about to end.

585
00:33:22.211 --> 00:33:26.204
The only way to prevent this
is through Akasha's destruction.

586
00:33:26.415 --> 00:33:27.905
But how?

587
00:33:28.517 --> 00:33:31.145
When she gives blood.
she's vulnerable.

588
00:33:31.320 --> 00:33:35.188
Whoever takes the last of her blood
will not survive it.

589
00:33:35.391 --> 00:33:37.052
What about Lestat?

590
00:33:37.259 --> 00:33:43.220
Lestat has joined with Akasha.
He's lost to us now. Forget him.

591
00:34:05.921 --> 00:34:07.479
My children.

592
00:34:09.658 --> 00:34:12.752
lt warms my blood
to see you all gathered...

593
00:34:13.295 --> 00:34:14.853
...plotting against me.

594
00:34:15.064 --> 00:34:17.498
-Akasha.
-Maharet.

595
00:34:18.300 --> 00:34:23.135
-You will address my king first.
-Lestat. what has she done to you?

596
00:34:25.774 --> 00:34:28.265
Lestat. step aside.

597
00:34:28.777 --> 00:34:29.766
Never.

598
00:34:29.945 --> 00:34:32.607
The world has changed
since you reigned.

599
00:34:32.815 --> 00:34:34.976
Then we shall change it back.

600
00:34:35.317 --> 00:34:37.444
Humans are animals...

601
00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:40.111
...brute creatures.

602
00:34:40.289 --> 00:34:45.522
-Their destruction can only make sense.
-We've found other ways to coexist.

603
00:34:45.728 --> 00:34:50.097
ln silence! ln shadows and shame!
And for what?

604
00:34:50.266 --> 00:34:52.325
For respect of mortals?

605
00:34:52.501 --> 00:34:54.662
They are nothing to us.

606
00:34:54.837 --> 00:34:56.634
They are merely food.

607
00:34:57.473 --> 00:34:58.906
Akasha. please....

608
00:34:59.108 --> 00:35:02.134
You think you can change my will?

609
00:35:02.778 --> 00:35:05.770
l've had enough of this discussion.

610
00:35:05.948 --> 00:35:07.540
Join me or die.

611
00:35:07.950 --> 00:35:09.645
l will not.

612
00:35:09.852 --> 00:35:11.649
-l will not.
-l will not.

613
00:35:11.854 --> 00:35:13.378
l will not.

614
00:35:21.564 --> 00:35:22.997
Do you love me?

615
00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:27.630
-Yes.
-Then prove it.

616
00:35:29.772 --> 00:35:31.171
Kill her.

617
00:35:32.241 --> 00:35:35.335
-She's nothing to me.
-Just the same...

618
00:35:36.312 --> 00:35:38.712
...l'd like for you to kill her.

619
00:35:42.585 --> 00:35:47.579
-You will not touch her!
-You still think to challenge me?!

620
00:35:50.926 --> 00:35:54.862
-Now.
-No. it's all right. Aunt Maharet.

621
00:35:55.731 --> 00:35:57.665
lt's what l want.

622
00:36:04.039 --> 00:36:06.200
How sweet.

623
00:36:12.381 --> 00:36:13.973
l'm ready.

624
00:37:30.759 --> 00:37:32.852
See. my children?

625
00:37:34.029 --> 00:37:36.657
Remember your real family!

626
00:37:37.966 --> 00:37:39.593
Or join hers.

627
00:37:40.869 --> 00:37:42.393
Now...

628
00:37:44.306 --> 00:37:46.171
...give me my crown.

629
00:37:47.843 --> 00:37:50.038
Spoken like a true king.

630
00:37:53.182 --> 00:37:54.809
Come.

631
00:38:05.027 --> 00:38:08.394
You see how he obeys?

632
00:38:08.864 --> 00:38:10.195
You will...

633
00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:13.760
...or you will all die.

634
00:38:19.508 --> 00:38:21.339
That is enough. Lestat.

635
00:38:31.253 --> 00:38:33.187
That is enough. Lestat! Stop!

636
00:39:41.290 --> 00:39:43.815
You kill me...

637
00:39:43.992 --> 00:39:47.018
...you kill yourselves.

638
00:40:32.107 --> 00:40:33.904
Wait. Lestat.

639
00:40:36.678 --> 00:40:38.168
You must stop.

640
00:43:13.135 --> 00:43:16.366
She drank Akasha's last drop.

641
00:43:17.773 --> 00:43:21.641
She took Akasha's death into herself.

642
00:43:23.045 --> 00:43:24.637
She's not dead.

643
00:43:25.614 --> 00:43:27.741
She sleeps.

644
00:44:26.341 --> 00:44:27.865
Hello?

645
00:45:00.675 --> 00:45:02.404
Oh. my God!

646
00:45:03.245 --> 00:45:04.735
Jesse?

647
00:45:05.947 --> 00:45:07.380
Hello. David.

648
00:45:19.060 --> 00:45:21.153
David. this is Lestat.

649
00:45:21.763 --> 00:45:25.790
-Hello.
-l have something for you.

650
00:45:29.638 --> 00:45:31.401
l believe...

651
00:45:31.706 --> 00:45:34.402
...that you wanted this back.

652
00:45:36.545 --> 00:45:40.311
Yes. thank you. Thank you so much.

653
00:45:50.625 --> 00:45:52.490
-Can l ask--?
-What's it like?

654
00:45:54.095 --> 00:45:56.393
Do you want to find out?

655
00:45:57.399 --> 00:45:58.889
Me?

656
00:45:59.067 --> 00:46:01.729
No. l'm too old to live forever.

657
00:46:02.070 --> 00:46:04.937
Well. if you ever change your mind....

658
00:46:07.843 --> 00:46:09.606
So this is goodbye.

659
00:46:10.579 --> 00:46:11.910
Yes.

660
00:47:11.139 --> 00:47:13.130
Hello. David.
